From d68336a3ddae7a44dfc3cf17e526e33d52906f0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suvojeet-sengupta <suvojitsengupta21@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:56:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf: lahaina: Boost yupik scrolls and animations less

At 90 Hz and above a scroll or fling held gold at 1.9 GHz, silver at
1.5 GHz and prime at 1.86 GHz, with an LPM bias and busy hysteresis that
kept the cores out of deep idle between frames. Every activity animation
pinned all three clusters at their maximum for 400 ms.

Floor scrolls, prefling and animations at gold 1651 MHz and silver
1324 MHz, the 90 Hz values, without boosting prime or holding the cores
awake. The floors only set a minimum; WALT still raises the clocks when
a frame needs more.

Change-Id: Id1d584c249619e44a8bfd0b2b8d96343e12623a2
